stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Owed: CS1 a statutory or file-format capture is written with no search
    [*] --> NotApplicable: CS5 statistic, filing, vendor page, repository, judgment or government publication
    Owed --> PartiallySearched: CS6 part of the amendment set is read and the unread part is written down
    PartiallySearched --> Owed: the row stays owed until the unexamined instruments are read
    Owed --> NoneFound: CS2 the ministry and date window is swept with nothing citing the base
    Owed --> Found: CS3 an amending instrument is located
    Found --> Regrading: every row resting on the base instrument is re-graded against the amended text
    Regrading --> NoneFound: the amended text is captured and its own window is swept
    NoneFound --> Owed: CS4 a new instrument citing the base appears in the watch feed
    NotApplicable --> [*]

    note right of Owed
        A blank field is not a clean search.
        Dependent rule versions cannot leave
        drafting while any row reads owed.
    end note

    note right of NoneFound
        One recorded search discharges every row
        resting on that base instrument.
        Fifteen searches clear forty-nine rows.
    end note

    note right of Found
        The link records both dates.
        Effective earlier than publication
        is the corrigendum fingerprint.
    end note
